maya: Quick FYI — I'm opening a docs PR to harmonize the SDK snippets for streaming + retries + pagination across py/ts/go. Trying to avoid the copy-paste drift we hit last quarter. PR link: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/3427 :rocket:

eli: Thanks — can you call out the breaking change for pagination cursors? iirc the TS example still used the old cursor shape.

maya: Good catch. The plan: update Python -> streaming async iterator example, TS -> ReadableStream example with retry wrapper, Go -> server-sent-events style streaming snippet. Also update pagination to use `next_cursor` (string) instead of numeric page.

sam: tagging @maya — happy to eyeball the Go sample. One question: are we keeping built-in retry logic in snippets or using a small helper util?

jordan: My vote: show a tiny retry helper so teams can copy/paste. Keep it intentionally minimal, e.g.:

```go
// tiny retry helper
func withRetries(ctx context.Context, fn func() error) error {
  for i := 0; i < 3; i++ {
    if err := fn(); err != nil {
      time.Sleep(time.Duration(100*(i+1)) * time.Millisecond)
      continue
    }
    return nil
  }
  return fmt.Errorf("max retries exceeded")
}
```

eli: +1 to helper. For Python streaming we should demonstrate `async for` with chunk-level retry (reconnect on transient). Something like:

```py
async for chunk in client.stream_response(prompt):
    try:
        process(chunk)
    except TransientError:
        await asyncio.sleep(0.2)
        continue
```

maya: I'll add those three snippets. Also updating the pagination code to show `cursor` semantics and a short note about eventual consistency when using caching at the edge.

docs-bot: New PR opened by maya: https://github.com/redwood-inference/docs/pull/3427 — labeling: docs, sdk-examples, priority-low

sam: For TS, please use the current SDK pattern we landed in the client v1.2: `client.chat.stream()` returns a ReadableStream and we should show both `async iterator` and `getReader()` patterns. Example: 

```ts
// async iterator style
for await (const chunk of client.chat.stream({ model, input })) {
  console.log(chunk.text)
}
// reader style
const reader = client.chat.stream({ model, input }).getReader()
while(true) {
  const { done, value } = await reader.read()
  if (done) break
  console.log(value.text)
}
```

maya: Perfect. I'll push the changes today, request reviews from @eli and @sam, and add a small migration note in the top-level migration guide. If anyone sees an edge case I missed (multipart streaming, reranking flows), ping me here and I'll fold it in.

eli: I'll review tomorrow morning. If everything looks good, can we also backport the snippets to the v0.9 archived page? some customers still reference it.

maya: Yep — adding backport checklist to the PR description. Thanks all :heart:
